KeePassPN
 * Feature: PGP has four tabs (Encrypt, Decrypt, Sign, Verify) and one input box; verify takes a pasted or picked signature and a public key imported for that check only, saved to the database only when ticked
 * Change: every PGP key import shows the fingerprint and asks before the key is used
 * Security: new databases use Argon2id with 64 MiB of memory instead of AES-KDF, older databases keep their setting
 * Security: a passkey needs the relying party id to match the page origin the browser reports, public suffixes such as co.uk are refused
 * Security: autofill matches the full page host, a subdomain entry no longer matches its parent domain or a sibling host
 * Security: the passphrase kept with the Keystore needs an unlocked device on Android 9 and later, old copies still open
 * Security: PGP keys expire after three years, use preferred algorithms, refuse SHA-1 and MD5 signatures and ignore revocations that don't verify
 * Security: PGP secret keys use the largest S2K iteration count for new keys, and your own keys are added as recipients when encrypting
 * Security: PGP temp files are overwritten with zeros before delete (best effort), and typed input is dropped when another PGP action is running
 * Security: the native key transform joins its threads and wipes its memory on every error path
 * Security: the entry picker ignores taps covered by another window
 * Fix: the Argon2 version is checked before it is clamped, HMAC checks use a constant time compare
 * Test: PGP round trip and failure tests
 * Change: the TOTP Summary folder uses the new TOTP icon, a transparent image shown in its own colors
 * Security: PGP clears its working buffers after use and keeps fewer copies of the passphrase and result text
 * Fix: a PGP key that was just made or imported shows in the list at once and is selected
 * Change: generating a PGP key shows a working state until it is saved, the done message comes only after success and a failed save is shown
 * Change: the PGP progress bar sits under the top bar, the selected key header uses the primary container colour, make and import have a card of their own
 * Security: PGP decrypt writes to a staging file and only shows the output after the integrity check passes; leaving the PGP screen stops a run and clears its files
 * Feature: PGP passphrase can be kept (Remember passphrase, wrapped with the Android Keystore) or asked each time; revoked and expired keys can't encrypt or sign
 * Feature: public keys can be loaded from a file too, armored or binary .gpg, up to 2 MB
 * Fix: PGP refuses messages with no integrity check (no MDC or AEAD tag), nested compression is limited to 2 levels, key and signature text have size limits, BouncyCastle 1.87
 * Feature: PGP screen from the + button: generate or import keys, encrypt, decrypt, sign and verify text (up to 1 MB) or files up to 50 MB with a progress bar, cache cleared on exit, keys are kept as entries in a PGP Safe folder
 * Fix: autofill suggests only sites and apps with saved entries, other login pages get nothing
 * Feature: while the database is locked, the unlock prompt shows only for saved sites and apps; two switches in Form filling (no suggestions when locked, saved sites when locked)
 * Change: sign up and change password forms get no suggestion, the save prompt stays
 * Fix: changing the master password works again, the new password was not saved
 * Change: the about screen credits hidefbi as the maintainer
 * Feature: Brand icons for entries: the icon picker has a Brand tab with the logo of the brand that matches the web address of the entry; the logos are stored in the app, so nothing is downloaded, and choosing one saves it as a custom icon of the database
 * Change: text styles and buttons of the import, settings dialogs, about, entry and icon screens now use the Material 3 components
 * Security: the AES key derivation loop no longer cuts the number of rounds to 32 bits, and the AES rounds and Argon2 parallelism are limited to the values the code supports
 * Security: turning on automatic submit in Magikeyboard asks for confirmation first, because the form is then sent without another tap
 * Feature: Import entries from a CSV, JSON or ZIP file (one JSON file inside), including Proton Pass exports, from the bottom of the database settings; every entry and group of the file is imported as it is, with TOTP codes as verification codes, other values as custom fields, dates as entry dates, and a count of characters removed because a database cannot store them
 * Feature: "Verify before editing" in App settings > User Verification controls verification for editing entries and folders (on by default)
 * Feature: Trusted browsers for autofill under Form filling; only trusted browsers can tell autofill the current website
 * Feature: Long-press an entry or folder for edit, move to folder and duplicate; entries can be reordered by hand when the group allows it
 * Feature: Verification codes (2FA) screen with import from Google Authenticator exports and otpauth:// QR codes
 * Feature: TOTP Summary folder at the top of the root group lists the entries that already have a one-time password, with their live codes; its name can be changed by long-press
 * Feature: scanned codes are saved only to the 2FA group, which sits second at the root, after TOTP Summary
 * Feature: About > Check for updates shows the installed version and opens the release page
 * Change: the free and libre build variants are merged into one; build with ./gradlew assembleDebug
 * Fix: undefined left shift in the SHA-1 and SHA-2 padding (found with UBSan)
 * Security: an old plain copy of a PGP passphrase is wrapped again when the key is used, or dropped if the Keystore can't do it
 * Security: an older PGP secret key gets the largest S2K count the next time its passphrase is used
 * Feature: your own PGP key can be renewed from the key list, three more years, same fingerprint
 * Change: the PIN check shows a progress bar and locks the input while it runs
 * Security: passkeys are offered only to privileged callers (verified browsers and allow-listed apps)
 * Security: saving writes to a temporary file first, so an interrupted save cannot replace the database with a partial file
 * Rename: the application is KeePassPN, package io.github.hidefbi.keepasspn
 * Feature: PIN unlock management in Settings > Device unlock (change PIN with the old PIN, disable PIN)
 * Feature: PIN validity of 7, 14, 30, 60 days or never
 * Change: three wrong PINs delete the PIN; two further wrong master passwords delete the database from the app
 * Feature: "Verify before copying" controls copy verification; user verification uses the database PIN, then the device credential, then the master password
 * Security: PIN wrap format v2 (Argon2id 64 MiB / 3 / 1, AAD bound to database URI and header)
 * Fix: a stale original no longer overwrites offline edits kept in the private recovery copy
